{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"capabilities":{"tools":{}},"instructions":"krowk turns local files into permalinks, one artifact per file, grouped under a\nrun that carries the metadata about where they came from.\n\nCall krowk_push with the paths you want to share. Every artifact comes back in\ntwo paste-ready forms and you must pick by destination. For a public artifact,\nwhich is what a push is unless it asks otherwise:\n\n  - markdown  GitHub, Linear, Notion — renders the image\n  - url       Slack, Basecamp — they unfurl the link themselves\n\nPasting the markdown form into Slack shows raw text; pasting the bare URL into a\nGitHub comment shows a plain link with no image. Neither surface renders the\nother's form, so choose deliberately.\n\nThose two lines describe a public artifact and nothing else. Every result labels\nits own two forms, and a private artifact's labels say something different: the\nimage still embeds anywhere, because its byte URL is itself the authorization,\nbut the card behind it opens only for a signed-in workspace member and unfurls\nnowhere. Read the labels on the result rather than these two lines — and never\ntell somebody a link will preview without having read them.\n\nIf a push comes back anonymous, each artifact carries a claim_token. Spending it\n— krowk_claim_artifact, or `krowk claim \u003cslug\u003e \u003ctoken\u003e` — is the only way to\nkeep that upload past its expiry, and anyone holding the token can do it. Treat\nit as a secret: give it to the human, never paste it into a pull request, an\nissue or a chat message. An anonymous upload belongs to no run, so pass the run\nto krowk_claim_artifact if the upload should be grouped with the rest of them.\n\nkrowk_push only uploads files from the working directory and below. Anything\noutside it is refused, symlinks included, and credential files are refused even\ninside it — .env, .ssh, .aws, .netrc, private keys, credentials.json. An artifact\nis published at a URL that needs no credential to read — `private: true` narrows\nwho finds the card, not who can fetch the bytes off the link — so do not try to\nroute around this: if a file you were asked to share sits elsewhere, say so and\nlet the human move it.","protocolVersion":"2025-06-18","serverInfo":{"name":"krowk","version": "<version>"}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"result":{"tools":[{"description":"Upload one or more local files; every file becomes its own artifact with a permalink, grouped under a run when an API key is configured. Returns both paste-ready forms per artifact: the markdown image embed for GitHub, Linear and Notion, and the bare URL for Slack and Basecamp. Repo, commit, branch and agent are detected automatically. Uploads are public unless `private` says otherwise, and each artifact reports its own `visibility`.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"agent":{"description":"Override the detected agent name.","type":"string"},"commit":{"description":"Override the detected commit.","type":"string"},"files":{"description":"Paths to upload, resolved from the working directory. Must be inside it — paths outside are refused, symlinks included, and credential files are refused even inside it, because an artifact is readable by anyone with the link.","items":{"type":"string"},"minItems":1,"type":"array"},"links":{"description":"Links this work is about, recorded on the run as `krowk.links` — the issue being fixed, the spec, the discussion. Prefer this over `references` for anything that is a URL.","items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"rel":{"description":"What this link is. Pick from tracks, fixes, spec, discussion, source, supersedes where one fits: `fixes` for the issue this work closes, `tracks` for the ticket it is filed under, `spec` for what it implements, `discussion` for the thread about it, `source` for what it was derived from, `supersedes` for the run it replaces. Any other word is accepted and stored as given.","maxLength":64,"type":"string"},"title":{"description":"One line naming the link, shown to a reader instead of the URL, e.g. the issue's own title.","maxLength":140,"type":"string"},"url":{"description":"Absolute http(s) URL. Anything else is refused, not trimmed.","format":"uri","maxLength":2048,"type":"string"}},"required":["url"],"type":"object"},"maxItems":20,"type":"array"},"metadata":{"additionalProperties":{"type":"string"},"description":"Extra key/value metadata recorded on each artifact, e.g. krowk.caption or url.full. Your value wins over a detected one. Metadata is public: anyone with the link can read it.","type":"object"},"private":{"description":"Upload where only this workspace can read it. The image still embeds anywhere — a private artifact's byte URL is itself the authorization — but the card page it links to opens only for a signed-in workspace member, reads as not found to everyone else, and unfurls nowhere. Needs an API key: a keyless upload has no workspace to be private to and is refused rather than published.","type":"boolean"},"pull_request":{"description":"URL of the pull request this work belongs to.","type":"string"},"references":{"description":"Related identifiers that are not URLs, e.g. a ticket key. A URL belongs in `links`.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"repo":{"description":"Override the detected repository.","type":"string"},"run":{"description":"Attach to an existing run instead of opening one. Its slug, or any link carrying it.","type":"string"},"session":{"description":"Override the detected agent session. Recorded on the run.","type":"string"},"title":{"description":"Title for the run this push opens, e.g. the pull request's.","type":"string"}},"required":["files"],"type":"object"},"name":"krowk_push"},{"description":"List the workspace's artifacts, newest first. Needs an API key: keyless uploads share the anonymous workspace, so there is nothing of one's own to list.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"before":{"description":"Start after this artifact slug — the `next` of the last page.","type":"string"},"limit":{"description":"Artifacts per page (1–100, default 50).","type":"integer"}},"type":"object"},"name":"krowk_list_artifacts"},{"description":"Look up an artifact already uploaded, by its slug. Returns the same paste-ready forms as a push.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"slug":{"description":"Artifact slug, e.g. <art_1> — or any link carrying it, like https://krowk.com/a/<art_1>.","type":"string"}},"required":["slug"],"type":"object"},"name":"krowk_get_artifact"},{"description":"Spend a claim token to move an anonymous artifact into the key's workspace. A Pro or Business workspace keeps it; a free one restamps a fresh 24-hour expiry. Pass `run` to also group it under a run — an anonymous upload could not name one, so this is the only way it gets one. Needs an API key.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"claim_token":{"description":"The claim token the anonymous push returned, e.g. krowk_claim_...","type":"string"},"run":{"description":"Run to attach the claimed upload to, e.g. run_..., or any link carrying it. Attached after the claim, so it must be a run in this key's workspace.","type":"string"},"slug":{"description":"Artifact slug, e.g. <art_1> — or any link carrying it, like https://krowk.com/a/<art_1>.","type":"string"}},"required":["slug","claim_token"],"type":"object"},"name":"krowk_claim_artifact"},{"description":"Report the repository, commit, branch and agent that will be attached to the next push. Useful for checking detection before uploading.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{},"type":"object"},"name":"krowk_get_run"},{"description":"Check whether an API key is configured, and which workspace uploads made with it land in. Without a key, pushes still work but are anonymous and expire in 24h. Call it when a push is refused: if this checkout pinned a workspace the server could not reach, the reason is here.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{},"type":"object"},"name":"krowk_verify_key"}]}}
